<title>CHILE: SOCCER-CHILE BEAT VENEZUELA 6-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-CHILE BEAT VENEZUELA 6-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile beat Venezuela 6-0 (halftime 3-0) in a South American World Cup qualifier on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Scorers: Ivan Zamorano (19, 26, 31, 47, 85), Pedro Reyes</p>
<p>(66)</p>
<p>Attendance: 42,000</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under played, won, drawn, lost, goals</p>
<p>for, goals against, points)</p>
<p> Paraguay     9  6  2  1  12  5 20</p>
<p> Colombia     9  5  2  2  15  8 17</p>
<p> Bolivia	9  3  4  2  14  9 13</p>
<p> Ecuador	9  4  1  4  13 10 13</p>
<p> Argentina    9  3  4  2  12  9 13</p>
<p> Uruguay	9  4  1  4   9 11 13</p>
<p> Chile	  9  3  3  3  17 12 12</p>
<p> Peru	   9  2  4  3  10 12 10</p>
<p> Venezuela   10  0  1  9   6 32  1</p>
<p>Playing Wednesday: Argentina v Ecuador, Paraguay v Uruguay,</p>
<p>Colombia v Peru</p>
<p>Note: top four teams qualify for the 1998 World Cup in</p>
<p>France. Brazil qualify automatically as holders.</p>
</text>
